        "source_path": "seed:manual_v2",
        "domains": [
          "Physics",
          "Computation",
          "Cryptography"
        ],
        "proof_strategy": "Define the boundary code as a stabilizer code [[n, k, d]] with stabilizers S_1,...,S_{n-k} acting on n qubits. Prove the AdS/CFT dictionary: each boundary qubit corresponds to a CFT degree of freedom on S^{d-1}, and each stabilizer corresponds to a bulk geodesic. Prove: S(A) = Area(gamma_A)/(4G) follows from the quantum Singleton bound because the entanglement entropy of region A equals the number of stabilizers crossing the minimal cut, which is the area. Test: for the [[5,1,3]] perfect code, construct the pentagon tensor network, show that the code distance 3 equals the geodesic distance through the center, and verify that the Ryu-Takayanagi formula holds for all 10 boundary regions.",
