        "id": "fd_0179",
        "title": "Prime-Indexed Spectral Stability in Expander Families",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists a natural infinite family of explicitly defined integer matrices A_p indexed by primes p (for example from Hecke operators, Cayley graphs over PSL_2(F_p), or modular-symbol complexes) such that the properly normalized second eigenvalue \u03bb_2(A_p) exhibits a non-random congruence-sensitive stability law: along at least one infinite arithmetic subclass of primes, \u03bb_2(A_p) converges to a distinct limit or oscillatory pattern not shared by density-1 subsets of primes. Test: Construct one explicit family A_p, compute \u03bb_2(A_p) for primes up to a large bound, and statistically compare behavior across prime residue classes; confirmation requires a reproducible residue-class-dependent spectral law that survives normalization and finite-size corrections, while refutation is failure to detect any stable subclass effect beyond random matrix fluctuations. Impact: This would reveal hidden arithmetic structure in spectral graph theory and could create a new bridge between automorphic/arithmetic objects, expander constructions, and complexity-relevant pseudorandomness diagnostics.",
