        "id": "fd_0363",
        "title": "Prime-Indexed Curvature Resonance in Expander Families",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists an explicit infinite family of bounded-degree Cayley graphs G_p indexed by odd primes p such that the discrete Ollivier-Ricci curvature distribution on G_p determines, up to finitely many exceptions, whether p is a quadratic residue modulo a fixed auxiliary prime q; equivalently, a computable curvature statistic K(G_p) has asymptotically different limiting behavior on the two residue classes p mod q. Test: Construct candidate Cayley graph families from groups like PSL_2(F_p) or affine groups over F_p, compute K(G_p) numerically for large p across residue classes, and attempt a proof via character sums and spectral expansion; refuted if no bounded-degree explicit family exhibits statistically significant and provable separation. Impact: This would create a new bridge between arithmetic information and coarse discrete geometry, potentially yielding geometric probes of hidden number-theoretic structure and new invariants for expander constructions.",
