        "id": "fd_0367",
        "title": "Arithmetic Resonance in Discrete Ricci Flow on Simplicial Complexes",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists an explicit infinite family of bounded-degree finite simplicial complexes K_n with integral weights such that a normalized discrete Ricci-flow-type evolution on the 1-skeleton Laplacian has convergence rate and limiting metric depending non-monotonically on the prime factorization of torsion in H_1(K_n; Z); specifically, complexes with identical rational homology but different torsion support produce asymptotically distinct flow spectra detectable after O(log n) iterations. Test: Construct candidate families with same Betti numbers and controlled torsion profiles, run/formalize the flow, and check whether spectral trajectories cluster by torsion support rather than by ordinary homology. Refutation occurs if spectra are uniformly determined by rational homology and local combinatorics alone. Impact: This would reveal a new dynamical channel by which arithmetic topology influences geometric evolution, linking discrete differential geometry, spectral graph theory, and computational topology.",
