        "id": "fd_0369",
        "title": "Prime-Modular Ghost Signatures in Betti Tables",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists an explicit infinite family of squarefree monomial ideals I_n over Z such that the multigraded Betti table of I_n after reduction modulo p is eventually periodic in n for each fixed prime p, but the period function P(p) is unbounded and determines a nontrivial arithmetic invariant of the associated Stanley-Reisner complexes that is invisible over Q. Test: Construct candidate families from combinatorial complexes with controlled torsion, compute minimal free resolutions over Z/pZ for many n and p, and check whether (i) mod-p Betti tables become periodic in n, (ii) the periods vary systematically with p, and (iii) no characteristic-0 Betti invariant distinguishes the same family. A single family with bounded degree generators and provably unbounded prime-sensitive period would confirm; failure of prime dependence or collapse to characteristic-0 explanations would refute. Impact: This would reveal a new arithmetic layer in combinatorial commutative algebra, linking torsion topology, free resolutions, and prime-sensitive algorithmic behavior, with possible consequences for complexity of Gr\u00f6bner/resolution computations across characteristics.",
