        "id": "fd_0515",
        "title": "p-Adic Stabilization Threshold for Iterated Barycentric Torsion Persistence",
        "description": "Conjecture: For every finite simplicial complex K and homological degree d, there exists a computable integer N = N(K,d) such that for every prime p, the p-primary barcode of H_d(sd^n K; Z) under iterated barycentric subdivision is eventually periodic in n for all n >= N, with period dividing p-1 except for finitely many bad primes determined by the Smith normal form of the boundary operators of K. Test: Compute integer homology barcodes of sd^n K for increasing n across many complexes and primes; confirm/refute by detecting eventual periodicity of p-adic valuation patterns of torsion intervals, and compare the exceptional-prime set against the boundary-matrix minors of K. Impact: This would create a new arithmetic-dynamical law for subdivision, give compression principles for integer persistent homology, and link combinatorial refinement to p-adic representation-theoretic periodicity.",
